# WHY THE THREE LEDGER PINS MOVED (2026-11-09, explained BEFORE re-pinning; cause shown in a scratch run, not assumed): the ledger template's board.pdl gained three BOARD rows (cols/rows/path, the geometry the new board page needs). The first ledger row records the hash of board.pdl + rules.pdl,
# so every ledger made under the new template differs in that ONE field, and so does the digest of the rows. The STATE hash (c69a00ab222f3bf2 for the 30-row game, d856979efae2ae51 for the 2-pet game) is the same under the old and the new board.pdl: no rule moved. Old board.pdl (git HEAD) gave e974d60c99abbe34 / 8718994e93e00b5a.
# The two rows below prove the cause and that protection still works: with the BOARD rows removed the SAME game replays to the OLD digest, and the ledger made under the new board.pdl is REFUSED once board.pdl is edited.
RUN | cp | $T/h/@.apps/demo-race/rulesets/default/board.pdl | $T/board_new_keep.pdl
RUN | sed | -i | /BOARD/d | $T/h/@.apps/demo-race/rulesets/default/board.pdl
RUN | $T/h/&.widgits/_shared-lib/ops/+x/game_core.+x | $T/h/@.apps/demo-race | $T/g | replay
EXPECT_EXIT | 1 | NEGATIVE-the-ledger-made-under-the-new-board.pdl-is-REFUSED-when-board.pdl-is-edited-(its-BOARD-comment-and-rows-removed)
EXPECT_OUT | the rules say | with-the-rules-hash-reason
MKDIR   | g_old
RUN | $T/h/&.widgits/_shared-lib/ops/+x/game_core.+x | $T/h/@.apps/demo-race | $T/g_old | new | 7
RUN | $T/h/&.widgits/_shared-lib/ops/+x/game_core.+x | $T/h/@.apps/demo-race | $T/g_old | join | A
